  "answer": "A balanced chemical equation provides several key pieces of information. First, it shows the reactants and products involved in the reaction through their chemical symbols and formulae. Second, it gives the ratio of molecules of reactants and products, which helps in understanding the stoichiometry of the reaction. Third, it provides the relative masses of reactants and products based on their molecular masses. Fourth, if gases are involved, it allows the calculation of volumes of gases liberated under specific conditions of temperature and pressure. Additionally, it gives information about the number of molecules and atoms of different substances involved in the reaction using molar mass and Avogadro's number. Lastly, it can also indicate the physical states of the substances and any reaction conditions such as temperature, pressure, or catalysts.",
